{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\norigin/main HEAD trips the C901 complexity ratchet added by c9f7 (scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check reports increased=1, so make lint exits non-zero). Root cause: commit aec1 (ff4c5600) raised src/rebar/llm/runner.py::PydanticAIRunner.run cyclomatic complexity from its baseline ceiling 24 to 25 via a success-path run-shape try/except. aec1 merged before c9f7, but c9f7's Verified gate ran on a pre-aec1 patchset; Gerrit's submit-time rebase stacked the gate on aec1 without re-verifying (ADR-0047 rebase-without-reverify hazard). A pre-existing failure of our quality ratchets on current origin/main; must be resolved before the epic's ratchet stories can close.\n\n## Approach\nExtract aec1's success-path shape-capture try/except (usage_log.run_shape + shape_only + telemetry-safe except) out of PydanticAIRunner.run into a small module-level helper (_merge_success_run_shape) that mutates the usage dict in place. Behavior-preserving; removes one try + one except branch from run, bringing its C901 back to <=24. No baseline regeneration; shrink-only invariant restored, not conceded.\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/llm/runner.py\n- tests/unit/test_usage_log_run_shape_aec1.py\n\n## Testing / Verification\n- python3 scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check exits 0\n- make lint exits 0 on current origin/main\n- pytest -q tests/unit/test_usage_log_run_shape_aec1.py (the success-path shape tests plus the new swallow-and-warn test) and the pydantic_ai runner suite pass\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] PydanticAIRunner.run C901 complexity <= committed baseline ceiling (24)\n- [ ] Extracted helper preserves the success-path key merge, proven by the existing tests test_the_success_row_records_the_tool_call_shape_too and test_the_success_row_carries_the_limits_and_duration_it_ran_under (both drive a full success run() and assert the shape_only keys/limits reach the recorded row)\n- [ ] The helper swallows a run_shape/shape_only failure with the same warning log and leaves the authoritative usage dict unchanged, proven by test_success_shape_capture_swallows_reducer_failure_and_warns in tests/unit/test_usage_log_run_shape_aec1.py\n- [ ] python3 scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check exits 0 against current origin/main (increased=0, new=0, stale=0)\n- [ ] make lint exits 0 against current origin/main\n- [ ] pytest -q tests/unit/test_usage_log_run_shape_aec1.py exits 0"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785966172717353001,"uuid":"3381b5f7-5481-4b53-b253-a8ce788c8240"}